# .assetsignore
#
# Cloudflare Workers static assets uploads everything under
# wrangler.jsonc's assets.directory ("." — the repo root, since Trakka
# has no separate dist/public folder). Without this file, that includes
# whatever npm installs during the build — wrangler's own devDependency
# install pulls in workerd, a ~128 MiB binary needed to RUN wrangler, not
# part of the site — which blows straight past the Workers 25 MiB
# per-asset limit and fails the whole deploy. node_modules is the one
# entry that actually matters here; the rest are excluded because they're
# build/tooling paths, not something a visitor should ever be served.
#
# .well-known/ is deliberately NOT listed — it holds the Digital Asset
# Links file the installed Android app needs to verify against, and has
# to stay servable.
node_modules
.git
.github
.wrangler
notifications
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
worker.js
